{"Title":"An Act to special education transportation reimbursement from 75% to 90% ","BillNumber":"S336","DocketNumber":"SD1785","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T21:27:37.23"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T21:27:37.23"},{"Id":"MPK1","Name":"Michael P. Kushmerek","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MPK1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T21:27:37.26"},{"Id":"AJS1","Name":"Adam J. Scanlon","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-24T10:41:28.0866667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S336/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Oliveira, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 336) of Jacob R. Oliveira, Michael P. Kushmerek and Adam Scanlon for legislation to special education transportation reimbursement from 75% to 90%.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 5A of chapter 71B of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out, in subsection (c)  the words “and transportation”.\r\n\tSECTION 2: Section 5A of chapter 71B of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “threshold.” , the following: Transportation costs shall be reimbursed at 90%.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendmen